// Push-to-talk cancel (ipc.md §4.7): the DLL stopped polling while the key was held (here: the
// window lost focus), so it sends ptt{down:false, reason}. The sidecar discards that utterance
// and sends nothing; the next normal press is handled as usual.
{"expect": {"t": "welcome", "profile": "test"}}
{"ptt": "down"}
{"sleep": 0.05}
{"ptt": "cancel", "reason": "focus_lost"}
{"expect_silence": 0.5}
{"ptt": "tap", "hold_ms": 50}
{"expect": {"t": "policy.set", "scope": "player"}, "timeout": 3}
{"ack": {"ok": true}}
{"expect": {"t": "say", "speaker": "copilot"}}
{"ack": {"ok": true, "applied": {"shown": true}}}
{"expect_silence": 0.2}
{"disconnect": true}
